  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nNW flow continues to become more amplified the next few days \nwith increasing ridging across the Rockies and high plains. \nTroughing off the Pacific coast looks to move ashore Saturday \nand flatten the ridge bringing increasing precipitation chances \nMonday and Tuesday. Ridging then returns for the mid and late \nweek. Could see some strong to severe storms on Monday/Tuesday \nthough there are still a some unknowns so wont speculate into \nthe potential too much. Overall seasonal weather with highs in \nthe mid 70s to mid 80s each day and peak daily heat indices \ngenerally 80-85 making a it a comfortable stretch of late summer\nweather.\n\n- Today\n\nA shortwave is quickly traversing the northwest flow aloft with\ncold air advection behind yesterdays wave helping to steepen \nmid level lapse rates. Overall pretty skinny instability but \nreminiscent of a springtime northwest flow with a deepening CU \nfield and the expectation for afternoon showers/thunderstorms \nonce we reach the convective temp in the low to mid 80s this \nafternoon. Not likley to see high rainfall totals but a few \nlocations in northwest Minnesota could squeak out a quick tenth.\nSevere weather is not expected with only 20-25kts of eff shear \nand 1000 j/kg of ML CAPE but some small hail is not out of the \nquestion.\n\n- Rain/Severe Chances Early Next Week\n\nSimilar to yesterday AI ensembles agree strongly on the track \nof the wave through the canadian provinces on Monday \nafternoon/Tuesday morning with the Euro still the more \nprogressive solution but the GFS is catching up as expected. \nOverall the expectation is for lee troughing east of the rockies\nwith MUCAPE in excess of 2000 j/kg to support at least a wind \nand hail threat on Monday afternoon/evening across parts of the \nDakotas. This does appear to evolve into a closed 500mb wave \nwith closed isotherms as well within the low meeting the \ndefinition of a cold core low supporting a localized tornado \nthreat in Saskatchewan and Manitoba Monday but given the track \nthis appears to stay well north of our area.",
